h of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=1$\n- The transformation is invertible" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308065 1113 #uuid "1c96229b-5c63-538e-82d5-2f8635304c00" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308065 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v+2 \\\\ 4u-3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v \\\\ 4u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=(-3)\\cdot 8-(-6)\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308067 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308068 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308069 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308070 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308071 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1041 "selection" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308068 13194139534758 true] [17592186308066 1110 #uuid "abb7c224-8364-5b78-9a32-3dc81a0265b1" 13194