ion can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v-5 \\\\ 2u+v+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308074 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308075 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308076 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308077 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308078 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1041 "selection" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308078 13194139534758 true] [17592186308073 1110 #uuid "308e64c4-063b-5783-8c9f-dea135b55caa" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308074 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308074 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534758 true] [17592186308074 1111 #uuid "2b7fe9fa-d6d6-5542-9e3b-97e770f792c4" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308075 1034 "I only" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534758 true] [17592186308075 1111 #uuid "d788609a-5bc0-515d-b00e-7fb366c70e9b" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308076 1034 "III only" 13194139534758 true] [17592186308076 1103 #edb/ref